### Hand-checked behaviours

* Diamond, single def at entry → **no phi**.
* Diamond, defs on both branches → phi at `join`: `(B, x.1)`, `(C, x.2)`.
* Simple loop → phi at header: `(entry, x.1)`, `(body, x.2)`.
* Self-loop `H→H` → phi at `H`; lone root self-loop → no phi.
* Unreachable block → under `unreachable`, no idom, no frontier, no phi.
* Parallel edges into a join → one distinct predecessor, no phi.
* Nested irreducible loop inside a single-entry SCC → `irreducible: true`, residual SCC reported, matching T1/T2.
